[size=140][u]Cargo Teleportation[/u][/size]

Capital ships waste minutes queueing for a pier just to hand over cargo to a station you own. This extension adds five research projects that extend the teleportation line to freight: your own L and XL ships exchange cargo with each other and with your stations where they are, without docking, and restock from your own supply ships and stations the same way.

[size=130][u]Features[/u][/size]
[list]
[*] [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Range I[/b] research, available after [b]Teleportation - Range II[/b]: a ware exchange between two of your L or XL ships happens without docking or parking once they are within 5 km of each other.
[*] [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Range II[/b] and [b]Range III[/b]: the same up to 15 km and 30 km.
[*] [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Stations[/b] research, available after [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Range II[/b]: every trade between your own L or XL ship and your own station happens without docking as soon as the ship is near enough to the station. Your existing traders and miners use it on their own, with no new orders.
[*] [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Restock[/b] research, available after [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Range II[/b]: when one of your L or XL ships restocks missiles, drones or deployables from your own supply ship or station, it gets the [b]Restock by Cargo Teleportation[/b] order instead of docking or parking: it moves within radar range of the supplier, waits while the supplier builds the items from its cargo, and receives them by teleportation. The wait is a few seconds plus a fifteenth of the normal build time, at most two minutes for an XL ship and one minute for an L ship.
[/list]
[size=130][u]Limitations[/u][/size]
[list]
[*] L and XL ships only: S and M ships trade, dock and restock as usual.
[*] Only trades in which both sides are yours. Trades with other factions dock as usual.
[*] Both sides must be near enough to each other for the game to count them in one area, which it calls a zone. Ships fly close to the partner first; for a ware exchange they then close in to the researched range.
[*] The ship or its partner still needs at least one cargo drone, as the game requires for any capital ship trade.
[*] A ware exchange that cannot complete this way falls back to parking as usual.
[*] The ship you are piloting yourself is left out.
[*] A restock by teleportation needs your own supply ship or station that already holds all the resources for the items; otherwise the game's usual restock runs. The game picks the supplier as usual: an own station only when the restock goes there, for example with the [b]Resupply[/b] order at that station.
[*] The extension patches four game AI scripts: [b]order.trade.perform.xml[/b], [b]order.dock.wait.xml[/b], [b]order.trade.wareexchange.ship.xml[/b] and [b]interrupt.restock.xml[/b]. The patches are small and placed with care, but another mod that patches or replaces the same scripts can still conflict with it.
[/list]
