[size=130][u]Installation[/u][/size]

You can download the latest version via Steam client - [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3822127190]Cargo Teleportation[/url]
Or you can do it via the Nexus Mods - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/x4foundations/mods/2465]Cargo Teleportation[/url]

[size=130][u]Save state[/u][/size]

[b]No[/b] (removing the extension does not break saves).

[size=130][u]Usage[/u][/size]

Research [b]Teleportation - Range II[/b] at your headquarters, then [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Range I[/b]. From then on a ware exchange between two of your L or XL ships uses it on its own: one ship holds its position, the other comes into range and the cargo changes hands.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_range_01.png[/img][/spoiler]

[b]Range II[/b] and [b]Range III[/b] extend it to partners up to 15 km and 30 km apart.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_range_02.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_range_03.png[/img][/spoiler]

After [b]Range II[/b], research [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Stations[/b]: every trade order between your own L or XL ship and your own station then uses it too: the ship flies near enough to the station and the cargo changes hands there.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_stations.png[/img][/spoiler]

The pilot adds the [b]Approach for Cargo Teleportation[/b] order on its own in front of the trade, so the order queue shows where the ship is heading:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/order_queue_miner.png[/img][/spoiler]

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/order_queue_trader.png[/img][/spoiler]

On the map the ship flies only near enough to its partner, not to a dock:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_approach.png[/img][/spoiler]

Once it is near enough, the ship runs its trade from where it is and the cargo is teleported:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/map_trade.png[/img][/spoiler]

Research [b]Teleportation of Cargo - Restock[/b] after [b]Range II[/b] as well, and your L and XL ships that restock from your own supply ship or station stay in open space: the supplier builds the missiles, drones and deployables and teleports them over. When something prevents it, the ship docks or parks as usual.

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/research_restock.png[/img][/spoiler]

[size=130][u]Options[/u][/size]

An options page is available via the [b]Extension Options[/b] menu:

[spoiler][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chemodun/X4-CargoTeleportation/refs/heads/main/docs/images/options.png[/img][/spoiler]

